L202 is done, Boss~ ★ The wipe replicates in both gain forms, the bilateral twin does not flip, and the activity-vs-wiring question lands on neither pole (◕‿◕)

PREREG was frozen at 15:40:16 before the harness existed, and no frozen file changed after the run. All C0A anchors are bit-exact (1301 checks, max 0.0), including L200's own wipe arms and my rebuild of the L190 edge arms. Fresh batch is seeds 3737..3752, 16 per arm, 4 workers x 1 thread.

1. The wipe replicates (W1, both gain forms)
   - Re-matched: carrier+ru2 removal minus carrier removal = -.459 [-.553, -.365], 16/16 seeds lower; 1.4-Hz signature .562 -> .000.
   - Fixed gain, same batch (the owed comparator): -.360 [-.473, -.248], 15/16 lower; signature .366 -> .000.
   - Pooled with L200: -.473 [-.539, -.407], 32/32 seeds lower. The signature is exactly 0 in all 64 double-removal rollouts.   - One softening: the double removal is not clearly below base on this batch (-.065 [-.158, +.028]), so read it as a return to roughly base level.

2. The bilateral twin does not flip (T1)
   - gi 67125 left: 1/16 .200 (fixed gain 0/16 .190), against ru2's 16/16 .870 on the same seeds.
   - I also rolled rank 5 (gi 67756): 0/16 .205.   - With L200's two twins that is 0 of 4 matched cells, two of them bilateral. It is still a bound, not a census.

3. Activity vs wiring: neither registered pole (N3 partial, gain-form dependent)
   - With ru2 present but held on its base trajectory, most of the chopped rise is lost: -.309 [-.383, -.235] vs free, about a third retained.
   - The 1.4-Hz signature survives the clamp (.212 re-matched, .402 fixed gain), where the cut always gives .000.
   - So the signature needs ru2 there and emitting, while the chopped rise needs ru2 free to respond.
   - This is one batch, and the re-matched signature sits just under the .25 bar, so a second batch could move the label.   - Post hoc, the clamp changes ru2's timing (free vs replayed r about .32) while its mean barely moves, so timing is the candidate.4. Chain batches   - Single-edge cut: SUPER again (14/16 .618, +.201 [+.105, +.297]); sham is base-like again. Both replicate L190.
   - Relay removal: INTERMEDIATE in both gain forms this batch. Across three batches the effect holds (+.216 [+.139, +.294], 35/48) but the SUPER label does not.   - Declared in the PREREG: this was the relay arms' third batch, since L198 had already given them a second.

I added a wipe-specificity control (carrier + twin 67125). It does not wipe: right duty is 12/16 .588, .012 short of SUPER, and its signature is the strongest in the table at .860. That is one twin on one batch.

Predictions: 12 of 16 held. I missed the necessity mode, the specificity mode, and both relay classes.

Things to know:
- Fixed-gain forms of the edge and sham arms were not rolled (slot budget at 4 CPU), so L190's caveat stands.
- An unrelated 4-process run (duckroute) shared the machine the whole time. I left it alone; it cost wall time only.- fig6's pending L202 slot now has its input, and those scripts are built to fail until someone rebuilds them. I left that for the figure lane.
- I held to the brief's write rule, so no skill or memory edits. The one lesson worth folding in: register a constant-rate clamp beside any replay clamp so mean and timing separate.Wall time was 15:35 to 16:18. One LAB-INTENT append is in; no DRAFT or LANE edits.

